      "message": "I don\u0027t think that these are needed.\n\nA classpathFragment that is used in an APEX should list the jars that it includes. Just like the i18n-bootclasspath-fragment does. It doesn\u0027t need to know the apex to which it belongs.\n\nSimilarly, a classpathFragment in platform_bootclasspath doesn\u0027t need to know which apexes to exclude as the platform_bootclasspath knows (thanks to https://r.android.com/1670067) which fragments it should include and which standalone jars it should use so it can make sure to only generate classpath information for those fragments that don\u0027t generate it themselves.",
